# **`npm ci` fails without this, so a fresh clone cannot install the client.**
#
# `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` 6.10.2 peers on eslint `^9`, and there is no
# successor to move to. `ui/eslint.config.js` carries why it stays.
#
# **It weakens every future peer check, which is the cost**, so
# `ui/src/eslintPeers.test.ts` fails the day that peer widens - the reminder to
# delete this file. Its silence is not evidence either: with this set an
# ERESOLVE naming a real conflict never prints, so a peer question is answered
# by `npm ls <package>` reporting one deduped copy.
#
# **At the root since the move to workspaces, and that widened it.** npm reads
# this file from the directory it installs in, and a workspace install runs
# here -- a copy left in `ui/` would be read by nobody and the install would
# fail with ERESOLVE. So the weakening now covers `server/` too, which had no
# peer conflicts of its own to lose.
legacy-peer-deps=true
